* Toppar stream file for benzamidinium, in the format the CGenFF program emits.
*
* NOT a cgenff/ParamChem run: the program is licensed and its output is not
* redistributable. Everything below is instead taken verbatim from RESI BAMI
* ("C7H9N2, benzamidinium cation, sz & pram") in the published CGenFF topology
* file top_all36_cgenff.rtf - the same atom types and the same charges, with the
* atoms renamed and reordered to match data/benzamidinium.sdf and the residue
* called BEN, as the PDB calls it.
*
* For your own ligand, run it through https://cgenff.paramchem.org and use what
* that gives you. A file like this one is what it returns.
*

read rtf card append
* Topologies generated by
* CHARMM General Force Field (CGenFF) program version 2.5
*
36 1

RESI BEN            1.000 ! benzamidinium cation
GROUP
ATOM C1   CG2R61   0.190 ! ipso carbon
ATOM C2   CG2R61  -0.115 !          H3   H4
ATOM C3   CG2R61  -0.115 !           |    |
ATOM C4   CG2R61  -0.115 !          C3---C4
ATOM C5   CG2R61  -0.115 !         /       \
ATOM C6   CG2R61  -0.115 !   H2---C2       C5---H5
ATOM C7   CG2N2    0.730 !         \       /
ATOM N1   NG2P1   -0.600 !          C1---C6---H6
ATOM N2   NG2P1   -0.600 !           |
ATOM H2   HGR61    0.115 !          C7(--N1(H11)(H12))(--N2(H21)(H22))
ATOM H3   HGR61    0.115
ATOM H4   HGR61    0.115
ATOM H5   HGR61    0.115
ATOM H6   HGR61    0.115
ATOM H11  HGP2     0.320
ATOM H12  HGP2     0.320
ATOM H21  HGP2     0.320
ATOM H22  HGP2     0.320

BOND C1   C2
BOND C1   C6
BOND C1   C7
BOND C2   C3
BOND C3   C4
BOND C4   C5
BOND C5   C6
BOND C7   N1
BOND C7   N2
BOND C2   H2
BOND C3   H3
BOND C4   H4
BOND C5   H5
BOND C6   H6
BOND N1   H11
BOND N1   H12
BOND N2   H21
BOND N2   H22

IMPR C7   N2   N1   C1

END

read param card flex append
* Parameters generated by analogy by
* CHARMM General Force Field (CGenFF) program version 2.5
*
* Empty: every term benzamidinium needs is already in the released CGenFF
* parameter set, and therefore in OpenMM's charmm36.xml. A stream file for a
* less conventional ligand carries the terms ParamChem had to assign by
* analogy, each with its penalty, and forcefill writes those into the ffxml.
*

END
RETURN
